  {
   "s": "IDEA",
   "n": "Vodafone Idea Limited",
   "cat": "Action(s) taken or orders passed",
   "when": "2026-09-16 17:52",
   "sent": "neutral",
   "txt": "**1. Most Important Fact**  \nThe Telecom Regulatory Authority of India (TRAI) has issued an order imposing a financial disincentive (penalty) of \u20b92,00,000 on Vodafone Idea Limited for failing to meet Quality of Service (QoS) benchmarks in various service areas for the month of November 2025.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**  \n* **Financial Disincentive / Penalty:** \u20b92,00,000/-  \n*(Note: Operational results such as Revenue, EBITDA, Margin, or PAT are not reported in this filing).*\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance & Forward Statements**  \n* The company stated that it is *\"reviewing the Order and evaluating the next steps in this matter.\"*  \n* Stated maximum financial impact is restricted to the extent of the disincentive levied (\u20b92,00,000).\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**  \n* **No action required.** The financial penalty is negligible relative to the company's balance sheet and operations.  \n* Shareholders may track whether ongoing network quality issues lead to recurring QoS penalties or elevated customer churn across affected service areas.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**  \n**Neutral** \u2014 The financial penalty of \u20b92 lakh is completely immaterial to Vodafone Idea's financials and operations."
  },
  {
   "s": "RELIANCE",
   "n": "Reliance Industries Limited",
   "cat": "Allotment of Securities",
   "when": "2026-09-16 15:48",
   "sent": "neutral",
   "txt": "### 1. Single Most Important Fact\nReliance Industries Limited (RIL) has allotted 12,00,000 unsecured, redeemable Non-Convertible Debentures (\"PPD Series Q\") of face value \u20b91,00,000 each on a private placement basis, raising an aggregate of \u20b912,000 crore at a coupon rate of 7.47% p.a.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated\n* **Issue Size:** Base issue of \u20b910,000 crore with a Green Shoe Option of up to \u20b92,500 crore.\n* **Allotment / Total Amount Raised:** \u20b912,000 crore (12,00,000 NCDs at face value of \u20b91,00,000 each).\n* **Coupon Rate:** 7.47% p.a. (payable annually at \u20b97,470 per NCD).\n* **Tenor:** 5 (five) years.\n* **Allotment Date:** September 16, 2026.\n* **Maturity / Redemption Date:** September 16, 2031.\n* **Coupon Payment Schedule:**\n  * Payment 1: September 16, 2027 (\u20b97,470 per NCD)\n  * Payment 2: September 18, 2028 (\u20b97,470 per NCD)\n  * Payment 3: September 17, 2029 (\u20b97,470 per NCD)\n  * Payment 4: September 16, 2030 (\u20b97,470 per NCD)\n  * Payment 5: September 16, 2031 (\u20b97,470 per NCD)\n* **Credit Rating:** CRISIL AAA/Stable and CARE AAA/Stable.\n\n*(Note: Operating financials such as revenue, EBITDA, and PAT are not part of this allotment disclosure.)*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Management Guidance, Outlook, or Forward Statements\nNone stated in the filing. The document only specifies that the NCDs will be credited to the demat accounts of debenture holders in due course and proposed to be listed on BSE and NSE.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On\n* **No immediate action required** for equity shareholders. \n* Watch overall leverage and borrowing costs, noting that RIL successfully raised \u20b912,000 crore of 5-year fixed debt at a competitive AAA-rated rate of 7.47% p.a.\n\n---\n\n### 5. One-Line Net Read\n**Neutral**: Routine, successful debt capital raise of \u20b912,000 crore at competitive rates (7.47% p.a.) under pristine AAA credit ratings, with no direct impact on equity dilution."
  }
